   323	tree were branches of one global irreducible prime `C`.  The proper transform
   324	of `C` is irreducible.  In the resolved boundary dual graph, its one connected
   325	vertex/subgraph attaches to the exceptional tree at the two sites.  The path
   326	inside `C` together with the unique path inside the exceptional tree is a
   327	cycle.  If one germ initially passes through an exceptional node, the first
   328	embedded blowup only subdivides that node and its attachment; it cannot
   329	identify the two sites or lower the first Betti number.
