   198	p_g(X_d)=h^0(X_d,K_Xd)=(d-1)(d-2)>0.                 (4.2)
   199	```
   200	
   201	Hence no dense open of such a smooth closure admits a dominant `A^2` first
   202	leg.  A surviving presentation of degree at least three must have a singular
   203	or degenerate infinity closure, a reducible/extraneous projective component,
   204	or an actual degree drop after cancellation.  Polynomial changes of Miranda
   205	basis can change presentation degree, so (4.2) is presentationwise, not yet
   206	an intrinsic invariant of the cubic algebra.
   207	
   208	## 5. The first nonlinear family: `d=2`
   209	
   210	A smooth `X_2->P^1` is a conic bundle.  Tsen's theorem gives a rational point
   211	on its generic conic over `C(P^1)`, so `X_2` is rational.  Its infinity curve
   212	
   213	```text
   214	H_infinity=X_2 intersect ({z=0} times P^1)
   215	```
   216	
   217	has bidegree `(2,3)` on `P^1 times P^1`, and is generically smooth of genus
   218	
   219	```text
   220	(2-1)(3-1)=2.
   221	```
   222	
   223	The rational-forest gate therefore excludes the generic quadratic-
   224	coefficient Miranda block from the infinity component alone.
   225	
   226	On the additional projectively finite smooth locus, for
   227	`pi:X_2->P^2`, Hurwitz gives
   228	
   229	```text
   230	R_pi=2A+B,          H_infinity=A,
   231	K_X2+H_infinity+R_pi=2A+2B.                          (5.1)
   232	```
   233	
   234	If `R_pi` is reduced, shares no component with `H_infinity`, and the pair is
   235	generic SNC, adjunction/intersection give
   236	
   237	```text
   238	p_a(H_infinity)=2,
   239	p_a(R_pi)=9,
   240	H_infinity.R_pi=8,
   241	bar-P_1=2+9+(8-1)=18.                                (5.2)
   242	```
   243	
   244	If the reduced pair is log canonical, (5.1) is ample and the complement is
   245	log general type.  If it is not log canonical, (3.1) is the correct test.
   246	Affine fixed-sheet information does not automatically control reducedness,
   247	common components, or singularities at infinity.
